{"cluster_id": "C-3750", "topic": "fsck's manifest-debris pass discovers namespaces via `store", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M-074"], "canonical_claim": "fsck's manifest-debris pass discovers namespaces via `store.listNamespaces` (`CasFsck.cpp:371`), which enumerates only `cas/refs/` and `roots/` (`CasStore.cpp:1640`), not `cas/manifests/`; a namespace whose only remnant is a staged `cas/manifests/...` body that `Build::abandon`'s best-effort cleanup missed (`CasBuild.cpp:958`) is not enumerated, so fsck under-reports it as unreachable even though the GC orphan sweep (which scans `cas/manifests/` directly) still reclaims it \u2014 a fsck diagnostics gap, not a leak.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-06-scenario-validation-night.md#notes"]}
