{"cluster_id": "C-3752", "topic": "A CI fast-test build broke because `dbms` linked the dead `ch_contrib", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-096"], "canonical_claim": "A CI fast-test build broke because `dbms` linked the dead `ch_contrib::crc32c` target left over from a phase-1a change, and the fast-test job does not initialize that submodule; the fix dropped the link so crc32c stayed google-cloud-cpp-only.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-17-unattended-stabilization-resume.md#L54-L56"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3753", "topic": "CAS GC's `gc_fold_begin`/`gc_fold_end` audit rows write only an anomaly count (e", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-124", "AUDIT-M2-152"], "canonical_claim": "CAS GC's `gc_fold_begin`/`gc_fold_end` audit rows write only an anomaly count (e.g. `{anomalies: '1'}`) as `detail`; `recordAnomaly` takes namespace, shard, manifest and reason but none of it reaches the audited row, so a firing cannot be identified or distinguished from other anomaly classes after the fact.; A `gc_fold_clamp` event (fields: namespace, shard, manifest, reason, at_version) was added per clamp occurrence to `content_addressed_log`, so that root-causing a GC clamp incident \u2014 previously an hour of event-log archaeology across archived server logs \u2014 becomes a single query.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-03-unattended-night.md#L171-L172", "docs/superpowers/worklogs/CURRENT.md#L784-L805"]}
