{"cluster_id": "C-3758", "topic": "`runFsck` labels `Reachable`, `Dangling`, `Unreachable`, `PendingGc`, `AwaitingG", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B002-068"], "canonical_claim": "`runFsck` labels `Reachable`, `Dangling`, `Unreachable`, `PendingGc`, `AwaitingGc`, `Unaccounted`, and `SnapshotOracleMismatch` objects, and `Unaccounted` is never used as a reachability input.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/04-ops-mounts.md#3-3-casfsck-runfsck-cpp-entry-per-h-96"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3759", "topic": "The strongest whole-pool test oracle is `runFsck()", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B002-140"], "canonical_claim": "The strongest whole-pool test oracle is `runFsck().dangling == 0` for no loss and `runFsck().unreachable == 0` after reclamation for no leak.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/06-tests.md#4-oracle-patterns-strongest-weakest"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3760", "topic": "`clickhouse-disks ca-fsck --disk <ca_disk_name>` opens the CAS disk read-only, w", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B003-059"], "canonical_claim": "`clickhouse-disks ca-fsck --disk <ca_disk_name>` opens the CAS disk read-only, walks live refs and trees through the production read API, and enumerates the pool prefix with paginated `backend.list`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/08-testing-and-soak.md#ca-fsck"]}
