{"cluster_id": "C-3767", "topic": "`claimMountAwaitingExpiry` accepts injectable wall-clock and sleep functions so ", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B005-062"], "canonical_claim": "`claimMountAwaitingExpiry` accepts injectable wall-clock and sleep functions so unit tests can advance a fake clock without real sleeping; production uses a system-clock reader and `std::this_thread::sleep_for`.", "issue_ids": ["S13"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-02-cas-mount-crash-recovery-design.md#claimmountawaitingexpiry--new-free-function-in-casserverroothcpp"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3768", "topic": "The corrected S02 workload uses deterministic incompressible `generateRandom('pa", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B006-038"], "canonical_claim": "The corrected S02 workload uses deterministic incompressible `generateRandom('payload String', <seed>, per_row) LIMIT rows` data with `max_threads=1`, so duplicate inserts exercise the real large-blob `dedup_head_first_min_bytes` path.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-03-scenarios-full-scale-campaign.md#L64-L70"]}
