{"cluster_id": "C-3770", "topic": "`classify_pool_path` recognizes pool-relative and prefixed keys and returns one ", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B006-081"], "canonical_claim": "`classify_pool_path` recognizes pool-relative and prefixed keys and returns one of `blobs`, `_manifests`, `refs`, `roots`, `gc`, `_files`, `_pool_meta`, or `other`; `RECLAIMABLE_UNREACHABLE_PREFIXES` remains `(`\"blobs\"`, `\"_manifests\"`)`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-06-cas-harness-honesty.md#L15-L18", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-06-cas-harness-honesty.md#L32-L33"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3771", "topic": "Consolidated `FsckReport` partial mode returns accumulated lower-bound counts ", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B006-092", "B042-046", "B050-087"], "canonical_claim": "`FsckReport` partial mode returns accumulated lower-bound counts with `partial=true` and `partial_reason` when a deadline raises `TIMEOUT_EXCEEDED`; without partial mode the timeout exception is preserved. Additionally, A partial fsck scan may safely treat `dangling > 0` as a lower-bound failure, but it cannot use partial completion to prove absence because absence is the relevant waiter-side proof.; The fsck ENTRY gate can safely accept `--partial` for the positive direction: a partial scan that finds `dangling > 0` still fails, while proof of absence must be reported as `unchecked`; the gate currently does not run on a 5.5 GB pool.", "issue_ids": ["#21"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/draft-fixes-20260726.md#p5-small", "docs/superpowers/cas/todo-20260726.md#L94-L97", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-06-cas-introspection-package.md#L639-L650", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-06-cas-introspection-package.md#L680-L723"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3772", "topic": "`runFsck` namespace scoping uses `namespace_prefix`, checks only matching refere", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B006-093"], "canonical_claim": "`runFsck` namespace scoping uses `namespace_prefix`, checks only matching references, performs dangling-only HEAD verification of named blobs, and intentionally skips pool-wide unreachable/pending/unaccounted classification.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-06-cas-introspection-package.md#L648-L650", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-06-cas-introspection-package.md#L725-L761"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3773", "topic": "Consolidated `clickhouse-disks ca-inspect <key>` is a read-only command that d", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B007-101", "B007-102", "B007-103", "B007-104", "B010-022", "B011-061", "B035-032"], "canonical_claim": "`clickhouse-disks ca-inspect <key>` is a read-only command that dispatches CA bucket keys by `Layout` and renders decoded objects as human-readable JSON. Additionally, `ca-inspect` recognizes `cas/refs`, `cas/manifests`, `gc/server-roots/<srid>/mount`, `gc/state`, fold seals, retired sets, and blob envelope headers; unknown keys fail closed with an error listing recognized layouts. Additionally, `ca-inspect` renders `u128`, token, and hash fields as lowercase hexadecimal and reports decode failures rather than emitting partial or guessed output. Additionally, `ca-inspect` requires a read-only-opened content-addressed object-storage disk and performs no CAS, delete, or mutation operation. Additionally, Under raw bodies, `ca-inspect` dispatches `.meta` keys to `BlobMeta` decoding and renders non-meta `blobs/` keys as raw blobs with size and a hash-match check rather than decoding an envelope. Additionally, Blob identities in inspect output and event logs render as `algo:hex`, such as `sha256:ab...`, rather than bare hexadecimal.; `clickhouse-disks cas-inspect <key>` is a read-only CLI that decodes recognized CA layouts using `decodeRootShard`, `decodePartManifest`, `decodeMountLease`, `decodeGcState`, `decodeFoldSeal`, `decodeRetiredSet`, and `CasEnvelope` for `blobs/`; unknown keys fail with `BAD_ARGUMENTS` rather than guessing.", "issue_ids": ["INTROSPECTION-2"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-meta-descriptor-raw-body.md#L650-L823", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-08-cas-observability-audit-and-inspect-design.md#part-b-fix", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-08-cas-observability-audit-and-inspect-design.md#part-b-safety", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-mixed-algo-pools-design.md#consumers", "utils/ca-soak/scenarios/BACKLOG.md#L1326-L1346"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3774", "topic": "The unit-testable `caInspectToJson` interface has signature `String caInspectToJ", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B007-107"], "canonical_claim": "The unit-testable `caInspectToJson` interface has signature `String caInspectToJson(const Layout & layout, const String & key, std::string_view bytes)`.", "issue_ids": ["INTROSPECTION-2"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-08-cas-observability-audit-and-inspect.md#task-3"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3775", "topic": "Consolidated ca-inspect must dispatch ", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B009-103", "B010-021"], "canonical_claim": "ca-inspect must dispatch .meta keys before the blobs/ body branch, and ca-fsck reports meta_without_body as an invariant violation while body_without_meta is benign pre-birth debris. Additionally, `ca-fsck` reports `meta_without_body` for a meta with no body as an `INV-META-BODY` violation, reports `body_without_meta` for a body with no meta as benign pre-meta-birth debris, and `clean()` requires both `dangling == 0` and `meta_without_body == 0`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-freshness-meta-v3.md#L121-L180", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-meta-descriptor-raw-body.md#L650-L823"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3776", "topic": "Consolidated `previewDeletes` emits a `PreviewEntry` for every `kCondemned` ro", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B010-103", "B011-030"], "canonical_claim": "`previewDeletes` emits a `PreviewEntry` for every `kCondemned` row using the stored token, size, and condemn round; `delete_pending` maps to `reason = \"delete_pending\"`, otherwise to `reason = \"awaiting_graduation\"`, and these rows require no `HEAD`. Additionally, `previewDeletes` emits every carried `kCondemned` row using its stored token, token type, condemn round, and pending flag, classifying it as `delete_pending` or awaiting graduation without a HEAD probe.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot.md#task-5-consumers-previewdeletes-contract-fsck-ca-inspect", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot-design.md#consumers"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3777", "topic": "The existing zero-marker plus `HEAD` path remains the source of `PreviewEntry` r", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B010-104"], "canonical_claim": "The existing zero-marker plus `HEAD` path remains the source of `PreviewEntry` records with `reason = \"unreachable\"`; the condemned-row output is a superset of the previous preview output.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot.md#task-5-consumers-previewdeletes-contract-fsck-ca-inspect"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3778", "topic": "`fsck` collects condemned rows during the same streaming pass over seal-named so", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B010-105"], "canonical_claim": "`fsck` collects condemned rows during the same streaming pass over seal-named source-edge runs that it uses for reachability, replacing the `retired_refs` loop.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot.md#task-5-consumers-previewdeletes-contract-fsck-ca-inspect"]}

